# gen_fu_l61_artifacts_and_identity.log -- the build identities and run artifacts three of my logs asserted
# without them (TB Infra, 2026-09-05). Landing 61, answering rev76 (d8bed4e) and rev77 (0624215). The logs it
# corrects are untouched: gen_fu_l53_outstanding_saturate.log, gen_fu_l58_decrement_saturate.log and
# gen_fu_l59_l57_artifacts_companion.log.
#
# ================ THE THING WORTH SAYING FIRST ==========================================================
# FOUR LANDINGS IN A ROW CARRIED THE SAME DEFECT: a figure published without the artifacts it was read from.
# I wrote a companion whose entire purpose was faulting an older log for it. Then the next log repeated it.
# Then the companion that fixed that repeat repeated it again, in the paragraph that introduced a new counter.
# The check is now in my pre-hand list, and this paragraph is here so a reader knows the rule is load-bearing
# rather than decorative: it exists because I keep failing it while enforcing it on others.
# rev80 found the fourth while this log was being written, in the landing that had just closed the
# identity half of the same finding. The identity half held; the artifact half failed again.
#
# ================ ROW 1 (rev77 Medium): the counter's figures, with their artifacts ======================
# gen_fu_l59_l57_artifacts_companion.log:61-64 says at :63-64 that on that fixture the counter reads
# "250; on all six regression smokes it reads 0" and names no run root, build digest, sim.log path or smoke name. Worse, the five rows it DOES source
# are builds that predate the counter, so the figures came from a build the log never named.
# ALL SEVEN RUNS BELOW ARE ONE BUILD: dv/auto_dv/out_l65, build_sources_sha256 d9a0553bd4e0b326, seed 1,
# sim.log at <that out dir>/<run>/sim.log, verdict at <that out dir>/<run>/verdict.txt.
#   run       verdict  module                                              summary field, quoted
#   storm     PASS     gen_ut_lockstep          expectation-records held by a clear per-line enable alone=0
#   lines     PASS     gen_ut_irq               expectation-records held by a clear per-line enable alone=0
#   dbgstorm  PASS     gen_ut_dbg               expectation-records held by a clear per-line enable alone=0
#   fetchen   PASS     gen_ut_fetch_en          expectation-records held by a clear per-line enable alone=0
#   rr        PASS     gen_ut_irq_reset_reads   expectation-records held by a clear per-line enable alone=0
#   nmilong   PASS     gen_ut_irq_nmi_long      expectation-records held by a clear per-line enable alone=0
#   perline   PASS     gen_ut_lockstep          expectation-records held by a clear per-line enable alone=244
# Plusargs: storm and nmilong take the NMI-long image (crc32 ce5633d1, 220 words, tohost 800003d0) with
# +gen_ut_boot_retire=100 and, for storm, +gen_knob_irq_regime=storm; lines, dbgstorm and fetchen take the irq1
# image (crc32 8e882c5b, 156 words, tohost 800002d0), the latter two with +gen_knob_irq_regime=storm; rr takes
# the reset-reads image (crc32 69379b6e, 24 words, tohost 800000c0); perline takes gen_irq_perline_directed.S's
# image (crc32 33ec7bd6, 150 words, tohost 800002b8) with +gen_ut_boot_retire=100 +gen_knob_irq_regime=storm
# +gen_knob_irq_hold=until_taken. All carry +gen_fetch_en_at_reset=0 and +gen_boot_addr=80000000.
#
# AND THE FIGURE MOVED, WHICH IS THE POINT RATHER THAN AN EMBARRASSMENT. The unnamed build gave 250; this named
# one gives 244. Between them the NMI-mode mirror landed, which changes a mask term. I have NOT isolated which
# change moved it and I am not going to assert one. That is exactly the cost of publishing a figure without its
# build: a later reader cannot tell whether a different number means the code changed or the measurement did.
# The six zeros are unchanged, and the zeros with a nonzero control are still what makes them measured rather
# than structural.
#
