# ================ ROW 6 (rev80): landing 60's red table, with its artifacts ==============================
# gen_fu_l60_nmi_mode_exit.log:47-64 states five figures and the ablation precision without the artifacts.
# rev80 recomputed its build digests, so the identity half is met; this is the artifact half.
# All three mutant runs are MUT-IRQWITHHOLDALL builds, module gen_ut_irq_nmi_long, seed 1, on the aligned
# fixture's image (crc32 3cba3f47, 218 words, tohost 800003c8, +gen_boot_addr=80000000
# +gen_fetch_en_at_reset=0); the ablation adds +gen_chk_irq_entry=0 and nothing else.
#   g_mut  <scratch>/l60b/rootG/dv/auto_dv/out_mut/g_mut/sim.log   depth mirror
#   h_mut  <scratch>/l60b/rootH/dv/auto_dv/out_mut/h_mut/sim.log   RTL mirror
#   h_abl  <scratch>/l60b/rootH/dv/auto_dv/out_mut/h_abl/sim.log   RTL mirror, named check off
# THE FIRE LINES, verbatim, which the log summarised as two order numbers:
#   g_mut  raised at cycle 902 (order 206) not taken within 17 records (now order 267, takeable records 18
#   h_mut  raised at cycle 902 (order 206) not taken within 17 records (now order 225, takeable records 18
# THE SUMMARY LINES, verbatim, and they carry the ablation precision rather than my assertion of it:
#   g_mut  bound failures=1 expectations released=0 open expectations=0
#   h_mut  bound failures=1 expectations released=0 open expectations=0
#   h_abl  bound failures=1 expectations released=0 open expectations=0
# So the ablation counts ONE bound failure while reporting ZERO errors. That is the precision stated as a
# measurement at last: the named check off suppresses the report and leaves the detection counted.
#
# ================ ROW 7 (rev80): the GREEN that was missing, and it is stronger than the red ============
# No run of the aligned fixture on an UNMUTATED build was recorded, and the six smokes never enter NMI mode
# with a nested trap, so nothing showed the design doing the right thing in the window the mirror is about.
#   nmiclean  dv/auto_dv/out_l65/nmiclean, build d9a0553bd4e0b326, same fixture and plusargs, NO mutation
#   verdict PASS, irq_entry 0, entries=2 nmi=1, bound failures=0, open expectations=0
# ENTRIES=2 IS THE POINT. The design takes the NMI and then takes the external line, and it takes it in the
# handler remainder after the inner mret: exactly the window the depth mirror masked and the RTL mirror does
# not. So the green does not merely fail to fire; it shows the design doing the thing the old mirror would
# have hidden, on the same fixture, with the expectation cleared by the entry rather than left open.
#
# ================ ROW 8 (rev80): the retained fixtures do not assemble as documented ====================
# Both retained .S files carry .include "gen_mmio_map.h", which lives in dv/auto_dv/tests/gen_programs/, and
# the directed recipe passes only dv/auto_dv/stim. As written the build fails on the missing include. The
# command that assembles them, and reproduces 218 words and crc32 3cba3f47 exactly:
#   python3 dv/auto_dv/stim/gen_program.py --seed 1 --out <dir> --directed <the .S> \
#     --gcc-opts=-Idv/auto_dv/tests/gen_programs
# The same applies to gen_irq_perline_directed.S and to gen_irq_mie_toggle.S. A retained fixture that does not
# build by the documented recipe is retention with a step missing, which is the same class as a retained diff
# whose header no tool accepts.
